# calibration_box.k26asm - a calibration shape, not a spacecraft.
#
# This asset exists so the mass-property derivation can be exercised
# against a solid whose analytic answer is known exactly, and so the
# assembly format has a worked example in the tree. It is a uniform
# rectangular box of 2.0 by 1.0 by 1.0 m and 1000 kg, for which the
# closed forms give, about the centre of mass:
#
#   Ixx = m (hy^2 + hz^2) / 3 = 1000 (0.25 + 0.25) / 3 = 166.666... kg m^2
#   Iyy = m (hx^2 + hz^2) / 3 = 1000 (1.00 + 0.25) / 3 = 416.666... kg m^2
#   Izz = m (hx^2 + hy^2) / 3 = 1000 (1.00 + 0.25) / 3 = 416.666... kg m^2
#
# It is deliberately not a craft. An assembly describing a real
# vehicle carries that vehicle's published properties with a
# provenance line per property naming the document they came from;
# nothing about a real vehicle is invented to fill a field, and an
# asset carrying a working figure it has not checked is marked
# unverified and does not ship in this tree.
assembly calibration_box
    frame x_to_port
    provenance mass "the shape's own definition, above" computed
    provenance inertia "derived from the geometry by the compiler" computed
    component hull
        mass 1000.0
        at 0.0 0.0 0.0
        mesh calibration_box.k26mesh
        collider box 1.0 0.5 0.5
    end
end
